    "title": "South Carolina women's basketball team dominates Southern University in first round NCAA tournament game",
    "text": "The South Carolina women's basketball team dominated Southern University 103-34 in the first round of the NCAA tournament on Saturday afternoon in Columbia.The Gamecocks started the game on a 15-0 run, which was their largest run to start a game this season. At the end of the first quarter, the difference was points in the paint. South Carolina had 14 points in the paint to Southern's 4. South Carolina led 19-6 heading into the second quarter.In the second quarter, the Gamecocks continued to dominate. Joyce Edwards had several buckets through contact and led the Gamecocks with 19 points at halftime. South Carolina's defense held Southern to just 19 points in the first half. The Jaguars were limited to 2-of-10 shooting from three point range in the first half and shot just 23 percent from the field before the break. The Gamecocks also out-rebounded the Jaguars 27-17 before halftime.The Gamecocks continued to cruise in the second half. They did now allow the Jaguars to score a field goal in the third quarter and outscored Southern 32-2 in the third period. The Gamecocks rolled from there. With the win, they will play in a second round game on Monday against the winner of the Clemson vs. Southern Cal game. COLUMBIA, S.C. —The South Carolina women's basketball team dominated Southern University 103-34 in the first round of the NCAA tournament on Saturday afternoon in Columbia.The Gamecocks started the game on a 15-0 run, which was their largest run to start a game this season. At the end of the first quarter, the difference was points in the paint. South Carolina had 14 points in the paint to Southern's 4. South Carolina led 19-6 heading into the second quarter. In the second quarter, the Gamecocks continued to dominate. Joyce Edwards had several buckets through contact and led the Gamecocks with 19 points at halftime. South Carolina's defense held Southern to just 19 points in the first half. The Jaguars were limited to 2-of-10 shooting from three point range in the first half and shot just 23 percent from the field before the break. The Gamecocks also out-rebounded the Jaguars 27-17 before halftime.The Gamecocks continued to cruise in the second half. They did now allow the Jaguars to score a field goal in the third quarter and outscored Southern 32-2 in the third period. The Gamecocks rolled from there. With the win, they will play in a second round game on Monday against the winner of the Clemson vs. Southern Cal game.",
